/-
Statement-only research draft: docs/RATCHET-LOG-DESIGN.md, §§2–4 and 9.
NOT imported by Minidregg, Kernel, a lake target, or any receiving path.
No theorem, axiom, sorry, crypto instance, or executable replacement is supplied.
Every declaration below is a Prop. Function arguments specify an eventual model;
they are not implementations or permission to treat arbitrary functions as live code.

Probability is exact finite counting, not an uninterpreted `Indistinguishable`.
For bounded executions, enumerate equally likely random tapes with `Fin tapes`;
pad unused random bits so both worlds use the same nonempty tape space. A strategy
includes the adaptive challenge-pair/query generator, its coins and its final bit.
`run a b tape` MUST execute the whole online game, not just the last root. Random
oracle tables may be lazily sampled from sufficiently long finite tapes. Rational
budgets avoid requiring a measure-theory import just to review the statement.

The `legal` predicate implements the ONLINE same-leakage rule of the design:
for every reachable common view prefix, both candidate operations have identical
released metadata and authorized answers. It does NOT require equal roots or
proofs and must not silently include the hidden target in leakage. Receipt hashes
are either excluded from this observer, explicitly equal leakage, or separately
protected. `budgeted` bounds strategy time, oracle calls, versions and proofs.
These definitions do not enforce those interpretations without ReceivingRealization.
-/
module

public import Init.Data.List.OfFn
public import Init.Data.Nat.Log2

@[expose] public section

namespace Minidregg.Kernel.BlindedCellHidingDraft

set_option autoImplicit false

/-- Absolute probability gap <= num/den, using both cross-multiplied inequalities.
An empty experiment or a zero denominator never satisfies this predicate. -/
def GapAtMost (tapes num den : Nat) (left right : Fin tapes → Bool) : Prop :=
  0 < tapes ∧ 0 < den ∧
    (List.ofFn left).count true * den ≤
      (List.ofFn right).count true * den + num * tapes ∧
    (List.ofFn right).count true * den ≤
      (List.ofFn left).count true * den + num * tapes

/-- Online leakage equality: a challenge contains BOTH candidate operations and
`choose` depends only on the common observable prefix. `reachable` must be the
paired-state reachability relation of the game interpreter, including its initial
pair and every allowed transition. `release` excludes challenged roots/proofs but
includes all authorized answer bytes and other public outputs. Its true/false
argument selects the corresponding candidate operation, not a fresh random bit.
This relation must hold even at prefixes generated by the simulation hybrids. -/
def OnlineSameLeakage {Prefix State Challenge Leakage : Type}
    (reachable : Prefix → State → State → Prop)
    (choose : Prefix → Challenge)
    (release : State → Challenge → Bool → Leakage) : Prop :=
  ∀ prefix left right, reachable prefix left right →
    release left (choose prefix) false = release right (choose prefix) true

/-- Target: indistinguishability of complete, adaptively generated transcripts.
The observable final bit includes arbitrary efficient processing of all views. -/
def TranscriptHiding {Strategy : Type} (tapes num den : Nat)
    (run : Strategy → Bool → Fin tapes → Bool)
    (legal budgeted : Strategy → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∀ a, legal a → budgeted a →
    GapAtMost tapes num den (run a false) (run a true)

/-- The missing model-to-code obligation. `reference` must be the interpreter of
§2's game over the new receiver/codec/prover, including failures, historical reads,
metadata and exact retry. An arbitrary toy interpreter is not this realization.
The intended instance additionally identifies each code observer with its game
view; it is deliberately not asserted for the present StoreHiding.items wire. -/
def ReceivingRealization {Strategy : Type} (tapes : Nat)
    (run reference : Strategy → Bool → Fin tapes → Bool)
    (legal budgeted : Strategy → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∀ a, legal a → budgeted a → ∀ b tape, run a b tape = reference a b tape

/-- Non-vacuity requires an actual budgeted legal challenge with different hidden
operation histories, not just an inhabited strategy type or legal reflexive pair.
`hiddenDiff` compares those histories, never the published random bytes. -/
def HasHiddenChoice {Strategy : Type}
    (legal budgeted hiddenDiff : Strategy → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∃ a, legal a ∧ budgeted a ∧ hiddenDiff a

/-- Root-mask guessing obligation in the uniform-mask / simulated-proof hybrid.
`bad tape` means an observer/simulator query hit one of T hidden outer inputs.
It excludes the honest publisher's own evaluation of its outer hash. Contexts
are unique per accepted version; repeated queries reuse that version's root.
This is a separate target lemma, not a premise supplied by a typeclass instance. -/
def MaskGuessBound (tapes lambda versions queries : Nat)
    (bad : Fin tapes → Bool) : Prop :=
  0 < tapes ∧ queries < 2 ^ lambda ∧
    (List.ofFn bad).count true * (2 ^ lambda - queries) ≤
      versions * queries * tapes

/-- Explicit triangle-inequality proof target. The intermediate algorithms are:
real = real masks and proofs;
uniform = independently uniform masks, real proofs;
simulated = uniform masks, simulated proofs;
ideal = independent uniform public roots plus simulated proofs.

fNum/den and zNum/den are *whole-game* PRF/RNG and adaptive multi-theorem ZK
gaps, not per-leaf assumptions. badRoot -> ideal is the ROM coupling obligation.
Primitive instantiations and those couplings must be proved separately. The
antecedent does not assume the desired two-world hiding conclusion. -/
def HybridReduction {Strategy : Type}
    (tapes lambda versions queries fNum zNum den : Nat)
    (real uniform simulated ideal : Strategy → Bool → Fin tapes → Bool)
    (legal budgeted : Strategy → Prop) : Prop :=
  0 < tapes → 0 < den → queries < 2 ^ lambda →
  (∀ a, legal a → budgeted a → ∀ b,
    GapAtMost tapes fNum den (real a b) (uniform a b) ∧
    GapAtMost tapes zNum den (uniform a b) (simulated a b) ∧
    GapAtMost tapes (versions * queries) (2 ^ lambda - queries)
      (simulated a b) (ideal a b)) →
  (∀ a, legal a → budgeted a →
    GapAtMost tapes 0 1 (ideal a false) (ideal a true)) →
  TranscriptHiding tapes
    (2 * (fNum + zNum) * (2 ^ lambda - queries) +
      2 * versions * queries * den)
    (den * (2 ^ lambda - queries)) real legal budgeted

/-- Statement (H), in rational form. Finite probability gaps are already <= 1,
so this uncapped rational bound is equivalent to capping its RHS at 1.
For independent uniform masks, take fNum = 0. No numerical budget is supplied
for cSHAKE, KMAC, or an existing Mini proof system. -/
def RatchetHidingGoal {Strategy : Type}
    (tapes lambda versions queries fNum zNum den : Nat)
    (run : Strategy → Bool → Fin tapes → Bool)
    (legal budgeted hiddenDiff : Strategy → Prop) : Prop :=
  0 < den ∧ queries < 2 ^ lambda ∧
  HasHiddenChoice legal budgeted hiddenDiff ∧
  TranscriptHiding tapes
    (2 * (fNum + zNum) * (2 ^ lambda - queries) +
      2 * versions * queries * den)
    (den * (2 ^ lambda - queries)) run legal budgeted

/-- Alternative (H-SM): a concrete fixed hash family keyed by its fresh mask is
assumed PRF-secure, with single-key gap pNum/den and reduction time sufficient
to simulate the other version keys. This avoids confusing a fixed hash circuit
with an ideal-oracle circuit. Binding needs its independent collision premise. -/
def StandardModelHidingGoal {Strategy : Type}
    (tapes versions fNum pNum zNum den : Nat)
    (run : Strategy → Bool → Fin tapes → Bool)
    (legal budgeted hiddenDiff : Strategy → Prop) : Prop :=
  0 < den ∧ HasHiddenChoice legal budgeted hiddenDiff ∧
  TranscriptHiding tapes (2 * (fNum + versions * pNum + zNum)) den
    run legal budgeted

/-- Specification of the complete opening RELATION, distinct from a verifier.
`validIndex` includes ordered/unique entries, honest subtree bounds/counts and
balance. `project` is the exact Lean-authorized query, including absence and
range completeness. No hidden sibling, salt or inner root is a public answer.
The live small witness relation must refine this full-state specification under
a held admitted invariant, without traversing the full tree at query time. -/
def CompleteOpeningRelation
    {Tree Store Mask Context Root Query Answer : Type}
    (logical : Tree → Store) (inner : Tree → Root)
    (outer : Context → Mask → Root → Root)
    (validIndex : Tree → Prop) (authorized : Context → Query → Prop)
    (project : Store → Query → Answer)
    (rel : Context → Root → Query → Answer → Tree → Mask → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∀ ctx root query answer tree mask,
    rel ctx root query answer tree mask ↔
      validIndex tree ∧ authorized ctx query ∧
      outer ctx mask (inner tree) = root ∧
      project (logical tree) query = answer

/-- Completeness: an honest opening can actually be accepted, rather than privacy
being obtained by a reject-everything verifier. Coins here are honest prover coins.
This deterministic target suits a perfectly complete backend; otherwise replace
it with an explicitly budgeted completeness error. -/
def OpeningCompleteness
    {Context Root Query Answer Witness Proof Coins : Type}
    (rel : Context → Root → Query → Answer → Witness → Prop)
    (prove : Context → Root → Query → Answer → Witness → Coins → Proof)
    (verify : Context → Root → Query → Answer → Proof → Bool) : Prop :=
  ∀ ctx root query answer witness coins,
    rel ctx root query answer witness →
    verify ctx root query answer (prove ctx root query answer witness coins) = true

/-- Structural binding obligation, NOT impossible global hash injectivity.
Two valid representations with the same public commitment either have the same
logical store or supply the concrete hash/encoding collision event. A knowledge
extraction reduction is additionally needed to obtain these representations from
accepting malicious proofs; ordinary statement soundness alone does not do so.
`collision` must be the actual byte-preimage event. -/
def BindingReduction {Tree Store Context Mask Root : Type}
    (logical : Tree → Store) (inner : Tree → Root)
    (outer : Context → Mask → Root → Root) (validIndex : Tree → Prop)
    (collision : Context → Tree → Mask → Tree → Mask → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∀ ctx t0 t1 r0 r1, validIndex t0 → validIndex t1 →
    outer ctx r0 (inner t0) = outer ctx r1 (inner t1) →
    logical t0 = logical t1 ∨ collision ctx t0 r0 t1 r1

/-- Local index preservation: logical execution, balance/ordering metadata and
all structural checks are preserved by the actual accepted update. The rejected
path and custody must not manufacture a post-invariant. -/
def IndexUpdateRefinement {Tree Store Request : Type}
    (logical : Tree → Store) (validIndex : Tree → Prop)
    (accepted : Tree → Request → Tree → Prop)
    (logicalStep : Store → Request → Store → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∀ before request after, validIndex before → accepted before request after →
    validIndex after ∧ logicalStep (logical before) request (logical after)

/-- Held balanced-tree invariant. n is live entries; no theorem may replace this
with a periodic full rebalance and keep the per-operation bound. -/
def LogarithmicHeight {Tree : Type} (validIndex : Tree → Prop)
    (size height : Tree → Nat) : Prop :=
  ∃ a b : Nat, 0 < b ∧ ∀ tree, validIndex tree →
    height tree ≤ a + b * (Nat.log2 (size tree + 1) + 1)

/-- Worst-case per-operation receiving cost, not amortized and not root-only.
The constants may depend on fixed security parameters and fixed schema, never n
or accumulated history. `work` includes executed index/crypto/prover/verifier,
allocation, journal and checkpoint work (within the declared RAM/I/O model).
`supported` includes successes AND refusals from valid pre-states under public
input bounds. `changed`, `payloadBytes`, `returned` and `ranges` measure
operation/output size; payloadBytes includes returned byte lengths too.
A fixed-size write with bounded accompanying queries is O(log(n+H+2)). -/
def PerOperationLogCost {State Request : Type}
    (supported : State → Request → Prop)
    (size history : State → Nat)
    (changed payloadBytes returned ranges : Request → Nat)
    (work : State → Request → Nat) : Prop :=
  ∃ fixed perByte perPath : Nat, 0 < perPath ∧
    ∀ state request, supported state request →
      work state request ≤ fixed + perByte * payloadBytes request +
        perPath * (changed request + returned request + ranges request + 1) *
          (Nat.log2 (size state + history state + 2) + 1)

/-- Standalone write target, useful before integrating the proof response path.
This target alone is insufficient for claiming law 17 for submit/propose. -/
def PerWriteLogCost {State Request : Type}
    (supported : State → Request → Prop) (size history : State → Nat)
    (changed payloadBytes : Request → Nat) (writeWork : State → Request → Nat) : Prop :=
  ∃ fixed perByte perPath : Nat, 0 < perPath ∧
    ∀ state request, supported state request →
      writeWork state request ≤ fixed + perByte * payloadBytes request +
        perPath * (changed request + 1) *
          (Nat.log2 (size state + history state + 2) + 1)

/-- The premise-inhabitation target is explicit. A reviewer must supply actual
hybrid algorithms and their crypto/representation premises, plus a useful legal
challenge. Supplying True for primitivePremises is not an implementation witness;
see the ideal-model sketch below and ReceivingRealization. -/
def PremisesInhabited {Model Strategy : Type}
    (primitivePremises : Model → Prop)
    (legal budgeted hiddenDiff : Model → Strategy → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∃ model, primitivePremises model ∧
    ∃ a, legal model a ∧ budgeted model a ∧ hiddenDiff model a

/-
SATISFIABLE / TEETH / PREMISE-INHABITATION SKETCHES (not proved here)

1. Hiding satisfiable, with a genuinely different hidden operation:
   two present hidden keys i != j, one unchanged visible key v, and two turns.
   Left: write i then i. Right: write i then j. Equal support, visible value,
   outcomes and all public metadata; no receipt event fingerprint is exposed.
   Choose the same public schedule in both worlds. In the ideal version use one
   independent uniform root word per version and an ideal complete-opening
   functionality returning only (root,query,visible answer,accepted proof token).
   On uniformly enumerated tapes each final event count is identical. Therefore
   GapAtMost tapes 0 1 holds for EVERY final test, and HasHiddenChoice is inhabited.
   Correct answered membership and absence queries are present; this is not an
   empty view or reject-all model. It is an IDEAL privacy witness, not a concrete
   binding hash scheme, cryptographic implementation or receiving-path instance.

2. Hiding teeth (one version suffices):
   start with two distinct hidden entry tokens; rotate only the written entry.
   Let the strategy's final test be equality of i's before/after token.
   With collision-free toy tokens, one world's event count is tapes and the
   other's is 0. GapAtMost tapes num den fails whenever num < den.
   Same test defeats a wrapped root when the ordinary proof exposes that token.
   For random d-decoy refresh the event gap is exactly 1-d/(n-1).
   Neither changed target is an allowed leakage field in this witness.

3. Premise inhabitation, without an impossible injective finite digest:
   use finite random-function tables for inner/outer hashing, independent mask
   tapes, and an ideal ZK functionality checking the complete relation. Collision
   events REMAIN possible and are counted, never assumed globally absent. Set
   fNum=zNum=0 for the independent-mask/ideal-proof version. Bound outer guesses
   by the finite-table bad-event argument; allowed budgets have Q < 2^lambda.
   Trees can be three-entry ordered balanced trees with genuine point updates and
   the common public schedule from (1). Thus primitive premises need not contain
   an impossible no-collision assumption. For the deployed algorithms the
   independent RNG/PRF, ZK simulation/soundness and exact representation instances
   are OPEN obligations. The ideal model does not discharge them.

4. Binding/completeness teeth:
   a constant commitment satisfies hiding but cannot satisfy useful binding
   with the actual collision event absent. A verifier accepting arbitrary subsets
   of valid leaves fails the complete-projection relation on a two-entry visible
   range with one entry omitted. A reject-all verifier fails completeness on the
   explicit honest visible-key witness. A local metadata checker that permits a
   false subtree count fails IndexUpdateRefinement. These are separate audits;
   a privacy-only satisfiable witness is not a binding witness.

5. Cost satisfiable / teeth:
   instantiate the counters with an AVL path-copy update of bounded-size entries,
   O(height) hashes/rotations, one outer mask, persistent history insertion, and
   linear-circuit ZK of the bounded query witness. LogarithmicHeight supplies
   constants independent of n. This inhabits both cost statements in the
   reference cost model. It does NOT establish those counters for live Mini.
   The broken sibling charges at least 32*n+44 bytes on every single-entry write
   (StoreCodec.rootPreimage_length). With H=O(n), delta=1 and bounded output,
   choose n=2^k; for any proposed fixed constants, exponential growth eventually
   exceeds the linear-in-k RHS. Thus PerWriteLogCost is false. Batch-average
   costs or a bound only on the root wrapper cannot serve as this witness.
-/

end Minidregg.Kernel.BlindedCellHidingDraft
